flowchart LR
    accTitle: Retrieval pipeline from source to grounded answer
    accDescr: Source material moves through extraction, splitting, and indexing. A user question and the index feed retrieval, ranking, and an evidence check. Sufficient evidence leads through context assembly and generation to an answer with evidence references, while insufficient evidence leads to a clarification request or a report that evidence is missing.

    A["Source material"] --> B["Extract and normalize"]
    B --> C["Split into retrieval units"]
    C --> D["Build searchable index"]
    E["User question"] --> F["Retrieve candidates"]
    D --> F
    F --> G["Rank and filter evidence"]
    G --> H{"Enough relevant evidence?"}
    H -- Yes --> I["Assemble evidence and question"]
    I --> J["Generate using selected evidence"]
    J --> K["Grounded answer with evidence references"]
    H -- No --> L["Request clarification or report missing evidence"]
